 CMo Library v1.0 — Cristian Mori

 THE CORE RULE: Business logic reads .Value only.

 Three signal modes:
   Normal:     Value follows hardware Input (optionally inverted, debounced)
   Simulation: Value follows SimInput (per-signal, for brownfield testing)
   Hand:       Value follows HandValue (operator override from HMI)]]></Comment><BitSize>448</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Input</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Raw hardware input (written by device driver)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>QualityInput</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Hardware health from module status (TRUE = good)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>8</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SimInput</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Simulation input (written by twin/test)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>EnableSimulation</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Enable simulation for this point]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>24</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SimulationIsActive</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Computed: EnableSimulation AND Common.SimulationEnabled]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>HandValue</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Manual override value (set from HMI)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>40</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>EnableHand</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Enable hand mode for this point]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>48</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>HandIsActive</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Computed: EnableHand AND Common.MaintenanceEnabled]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>56</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Value</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Conditioned, filtered, mode-selected result]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Inverted</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Invert input polarity]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>BadQualityValue</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Value to use when quality is bad (safe state)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>80</BitOffs></Sub